`makeLexiconDecision` always returns the base `LexiconDecision` type, which means callers that need `BashLockdownDecision` or `ReportScopeDecision` cannot use this safe constructor directly — they must either use a type assertion (losing type safety) or manually construct the object (bypassing the alias-sync mechanism entirely). Consider adding a generic overload so the narrowed types can also be built through the synced constructor:

```typescript
export function makeLexiconDecision(
  base: Pick<LexiconDecision, 'verdict' | 'pattern' | 'token' | 'message' | 'mPSE'> & { resolvedDir?: string },
): LexiconDecision;
export function makeLexiconDecision<T extends 'ALLOW_READ' | 'BLOCKED'>(
  base: Pick<BashLockdownDecision, 'verdict' | 'pattern' | 'token' | 'message' | 'mPSE'> & { verdict: T } & { resolvedDir?: string },
): BashLockdownDecision;
// (or a simpler generic approach)
```
Alternatively, provide dedicated factory functions like `makeBashLockdownDecision` and `makeReportScopeDecision` that return the narrowed types while still enforcing alias consistency.

