comments.content:
The comment on line 102 describes this as an "LRU, 500 files" cache, but the eviction strategy is FIFO, not LRU. When a cached file is accessed again, the `if (!lines)` branch is not taken, so the Map entry is NOT moved to the end of the insertion-ordered Map. Eviction always removes the oldest-inserted entry (`Map.keys().next().value`), regardless of how recently it was accessed. This means a hot file inserted early can be evicted while a cold file inserted later persists — the opposite of LRU behavior.

To achieve true LRU, a cached hit should re-insert the entry at the end of the Map:
```ts
let lines = edgeEvidenceLineCache.get(file);
if (lines) {
  // Promote to most-recently-used position
  edgeEvidenceLineCache.delete(file);
  edgeEvidenceLineCache.set(file, lines);
} else {
  // ... existing insertion logic
}
```
Alternatively, if FIFO is the intended behavior, the comment should be corrected to say "FIFO" instead of "LRU" to avoid misleading future maintainers.

